# requirements/stellar/companions.ears
capability: Hidden companions of star-cluster members
owner: stellar
requirements:
  - id: STL-020
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall compute each Gaia orbit's photocentre size, astrometric mass function and dark-partner mass, and call a partner a neutron star or black hole only when Gaia found no main-sequence flux ratio for it (or put it in AMRF class III) and Gaia's lower mass bound is above the Chandrasekhar mass."
    rationale: "Gaia's binary_masses lower bound carries the orbit's full covariance; SDP's own Kepler arithmetic is reported beside it (Gaia BH1 gives 12.8 solar masses both ways). Only Orbital+M1 combinations are judged, because Gaia documents m2_lower for them (DR3 data model, read 2026-11-04)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_the_thiele_innes_elements_give_back_the_orbits_size_whatever_its_orientation"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_keplers_law_gives_back_the_partners_mass"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_the_mass_solver_is_exact_from_tiny_to_huge_mass_functions_and_refuses_bad_input"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_only_a_dark_partner_above_the_chandrasekhar_mass_is_a_neutron_star_or_black_hole"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_an_orbit_of_another_kind_or_too_weak_is_not_used"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_a_cluster_distance_moves_gaias_lower_bound_and_nearer_means_lighter"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_the_settings_are_hashed_for_every_report"
  - id: STL-021
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall measure the field's wobble baseline (median and 1.4826 times the median absolute deviation of log RUWE per G bin) and the field shares of wobblers and flagged orbits per G and parallax bin, and give a Poisson tail for a cluster's counts against the sum of its members' field shares."
    rationale: "The null is the field itself: a cluster is remarkable only if it holds more wobblers or dark partners than stars of the same brightness and distance elsewhere."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_the_wobble_baseline_is_the_fields_own_median_and_spread_at_each_brightness"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_the_field_share_of_wobblers_is_counted_from_the_same_histogram"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_the_poisson_tail_says_how_often_the_field_gives_as_many"
  - id: STL-022
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The stellar module shall find each cluster's members again from its seed members' footprint, motion and parallax, without reading RUWE, and judge every member's Gaia orbit at the cluster's parallax."
    rationale: "The sweep's catalogue drops high-RUWE stars, which are the ones that wobble; a shared cluster distance is more precise than one star's parallax (as cmd_policy cluster-distance)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_members_are_found_again_blind_to_ruwe"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_the_second_scan_keeps_only_stars_inside_a_footprint"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_a_dark_partner_of_a_member_is_found_and_the_cluster_is_judged_against_the_field"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_a_cluster_with_too_few_seeds_in_the_scan_is_reported_not_screened"
      - "python/tests.stellar.test_companions::test_clusters_come_from_sweep_tiles_once_each_or_from_a_member_list"
  - id: STL-023
    pattern: event
    text: "When `sdp companions field` or `sdp companions screen` is invoked, the system shall write the flagged orbits (and for a screen each cluster's counts) to CSV files with a summary marked EXPLORATORY, reading clusters from sweep tiles or a member list and stars from the complete bulk Gaia copy in two passes."
    rationale: "The Gaia DR3 trial of the screen the Gaia DR4 run will use; the field list carries the known-answer check that Gaia BH1 is flagged."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_companions::test_the_field_list_flags_gaia_bh1_and_says_so"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_companions::test_a_screen_finds_the_dark_partner_of_a_member_the_sweep_left_out"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_companions::test_a_screen_needs_one_source_of_clusters_and_a_fetched_orbit_table"
      - "python/tests.cli.test_cli_companions::test_fetch_writes_the_orbit_table_through_the_transport"
